<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qian Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">929–988</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qian Chu was the last king of Wuyue, the coastal kingdom around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a>, reigning from 947 to 978. He helped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song dynasty</a> conquer Southern Tang and in 978 handed his entire kingdom to Song without a fight, so that Wuyue's lands were spared war. He was honoured with titles at the Song court for the rest of his life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qian-chu.jpg" alt="Qian Chu" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 松照庵 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Qian_Hongchu_King_Zhongyi_of_Wuyue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
